# Flutter writes LF. With core.autocrlf=true on Windows the checkout is CRLF, so every
# `flutter pub get` rewrote the generated plugin registrants to LF and git showed seven files
# modified with no content change. Pinning the folder to LF makes the checkout match what
# Flutter writes. text=auto, not text: the folder holds binaries (icons, images) that a plain
# `text` rule would corrupt.
lmslocal-flutter/** text=auto eol=lf
